  "body": "Seen in the regenerated shell snapshot for the 0.18.0 cut (`crates/ui/tests/snapshots/egui_app.png`, 1280 px wide), compared with the 0.17.0 golden:\n\n- Ribbon labels are truncated: \"Save As\" -> \"Sav…\", \"Setups\" -> \"Set…\", \"Milling 2D\" / \"Milling 3D\" / \"Milling…\" -> three adjacent buttons that all read \"Milli…\", \"Drilling\" -> \"Drill…\", \"Multi-axis\" -> \"Mul…\", \"Simulate\" -> \"Sim…\", \"Deviate\" -> \"Devi…\", \"Panels\" -> \"Pan…\", \"Theme\" -> \"The…\". A user cannot tell the three \"Milli…\" buttons apart without hovering.\n- The group captions under the ribbon (File, Setup, Milling 2D, Milling 3D, Drilling, Multi-axis, Modify, Inspect, View) are no longer drawn. The review of PR #767 noted `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs:1135` `let _ = captions;` - the caption geometry is computed and never painted.\n\nSince: PR #767 (UI polish, merged 2026-11-11). The 0.17.0 golden shows the full labels (some overlapping) and the captions.\n\nExpected: every ribbon button is identifiable at the default 1280 px window - full labels, or a deliberate short label per button (not a cut-off one), and the group captions back, or removed on purpose with a decision entry. Text in plain English.\n\nAlso from #767's review, same area: `crates/ui/src/interact.rs:731-740` - a non-finite camera target or distance could make the ground-grid loop effectively hang; add a finite guard (Prime Directive: no hang).\n\nDone means: a structural assertion (not a PNG) pins that no ribbon label is elided at 1280 px and that two buttons never show the same text; the captions are asserted present or their removal is recorded; the grid loop has its guard and a test with a NaN camera.\n",
